# L §4.4, §5.18 (tally 2.1.8 R13, #186): a diff under windows each whose set of lines differs by sub-window prints one
# block per run of sub-windows that agree, each under its head, then its lines. bonus_amt is read at wd; sc raises
# the April rate, so the diff changes only where wd falls in April.
# 2.1.7's refcore printed the first day's diff unlabelled; the engine stopped "not built".
=== base.tally
model w_each
  tally 2
  on 2026-03-01
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31

source card "invented"
unit PLN: currency minor 0.01

axis ax
  lo "low"
  hi "high"

input wd: date
input rate: money PLN
input twice: int

def bonus_amt: money PLN at wd
  rule base = rate
  rule hi beats base = rate * twice when ax == hi

version v
  cite card
  governs always
  known 2026-01-01
  wd = window(2026-03-28, 2026-04-03) "c"
  twice = 2 "c"

version r1
  cite card
  governs ..2026-03-31
  known 2026-01-01
  rate = 10.00 PLN "c"

version r2
  cite card
  governs 2026-04-01..
  known 2026-01-01
  rate = 12.00 PLN "c"

ask d1: diff(bonus_amt) in sc against w_each with ax = hi windows each
=== sc.tally
scenario sc over w_each
  tally 2
  from 2026-01-01
  note "x"

version vs
  cite card
  governs 2026-04-01..
  known 2026-01-01
  replace rate = 15.00 PLN "c"
=== expect
d1 [wd = 2026-03-28 .. 2026-03-31]: diff in sc against w_each: 0 changed, 0 added, 0 removed, 1 unchanged
  pinned: ax = hi
  world: sc
  world: w_each
  cut 2026-03-01
d1 [wd = 2026-04-01 .. 2026-04-03]: diff in sc against w_each: 1 changed, 0 added, 0 removed, 0 unchanged
  changed bonus_amt: 30.00 PLN against 24.00 PLN
  pinned: ax = hi
  world: sc
  world: w_each
  held: rate = 12.00 PLN (r2), read for 2026-04-01
  held: rate = 12.00 PLN (r2), read for 2026-04-02
  held: rate = 12.00 PLN (r2), read for 2026-04-03
  held: rate = 15.00 PLN (vs), read for 2026-04-01
  held: rate = 15.00 PLN (vs), read for 2026-04-02
  held: rate = 15.00 PLN (vs), read for 2026-04-03
  cut 2026-03-01
